A||||2||87GT||My Trip to Colorado||||1||
Z||000000||87GT||05-14-2000||01:16 PM||||I went to Colorado Springs, CO this past week for  a software conference and while I was there, I was looking for fieros!  I was there a week and saw about 12 fieros riding around.  I remember one in particular that was a black SE.  It was in a parking lot right next to where I had class for this software.  This past Friday, I was walking thru the parking lot to get to the building and the person that owned this car was pulling out of the lot with a friend I assume with him.  He drove right passed me and I waved at him.  I dont know if he noticed my Fiero shirt I was wearing.  Anyways, his car looked great!  The other fieros I saw were: 86 Gold SC, 88 Red GT, 87 maroon GT, 85GT black, 84 Black SC, 85GT Red, ummm...  I saw about 4 white 84-85 sport coupe/se's going down the road, and I saw a GT that was grey, and had a ground affects trim on it.  It was pretty loud, I dont know what he did to it.  Anyways, for those of you that havent been to CO, go!  It was absolutely awesome out there.  Im from Florida and going to a place that has mountains is something else to see.  I wanna go back!||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||05-14-2000||02:42 PM||||I forgot to mention that we flew out of Denver and I saw a couple of fieros in a suburb called Loveland.  One was a 88GT in red, and the other was a 85GT that said, FIERO GT on the doors.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-14-2000||05:37 PM||||You should have said you were coming!!  We would have shown you a lot more Fieros.  <P>You are right about Colorado.....it is a very beautiful state.  I'm entering my 17th year here and don't plan on leaving anytime soon.<P>Let us know next time you're in town.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
